abstract: >-
  RDFS ontology and SHACL shapes encoding selected clauses of Indonesia's Law No. 27 of 2022
  on Personal Data Protection, synthetic test graphs with answer keys, verification scripts
  (equivalence class partitioning, boundary value analysis, trigger and mutation tests),
  the official verification and performance results, the operability screening of all 76
  articles, and anonymized legal alignment ratings. The shapes are validated with pySHACL
  using RDFS entailment. The test data are synthetic; the results show that the rules behave
  as designed and do not establish compliance by any real organization.
